    flat_ast_bridge_phase3_snapshot_throughput_2026-08-31, 0, "2026-11-28 p3sweep6: measured on the interpreted lane (quiet box): legacy 20.6/88.1/353.5 ms at 100/400/1600 fns; scoped 6.1/28.0/130.7 ms (3.37x/3.15x/2.71x). Root cause: every flat-AST getter crossed into the SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_* process-env mirror (~29 crossings/declaration; 11606/conversion at 400 fns measured via a runtime diagnostic counter), each an interpreter->SFFI round trip. Fix: flat_ast_to_module wraps the conversion in a scope (env-mirror lane only) forcing decl/stmt/expr/module-decl getters onto the arena arrays (written in lockstep; the cache hit path already converts from arrays alone) + a same-module control-flag cache; kill switch SIMPLE_FLAT_BRIDGE_ARENA_SCOPE=0; flat_ast_to_module made pub (facade already exported it). Deliberate deviation: the doc candidate's per-file dump+restore admission costs 0.6-0.8s at 1600 decls - 2-5x the entire legacy conversion - not used; codec untouched. Verification: spec 4/4 (parity incl HIR encode blob equality + extend state + diagnostics); perf lane PROBE 4.22x; counter scoped=6 vs legacy=11606; direct-env-runtime-guard PASS; scratch seed build no new warnings. Residuals: codec roundtrip selftest PASS but the full roundtrip build needs the next bootstrap deploy; RSS bound unmeasured (memory_usage unavailable in the seed lane); the 3x gate asserted at 400 fns (2.71x at 1600 documented); control-flag cache must live in the consumer module (cross-module copy read a different interpreter instance - documented). close_evidence reproducer=test/05_perf/compiler/flat_bridge_arena_scope_spec.spl prevention=src/compiler/10.frontend/_FlatAstBridge/module_assembly.spl"

